rogress and when you see those X's  coming on you don't want to break the  chain so you want to keep going every  day we number four would say you  saturday is a cheat day and that was  when I could eat whatever I wanted you  know there was no calorie restrictions I  just ate ate ate ate ate ate ate but I  still had to keep my chain so I still  was running for 30 minutes in the day  and I was still fasting until noon this  was one of the hardest things because I  get this delicious doughnut from Tim  Hortons or this breakfast that ends at  noon and so I really wanted to eat that  so he buy it a couple minutes early I'd  be sitting there looking at my doughnut  like I got five minutes left before I  can eat this thing  and then once noon came look show it in  so Saturday is my cheat day but I still  am on my fast until noon it's 15 minutes  till noon and I'm excited to dig into my  Boston cream doing it this is gonna be a  brutal 15 minutes I love it so that  really helped that helps it helps on a  psychological level to have one day when  you can eat whatever you want and I  think there is also a lot of research  that backs up having a cheat day to kind  of spike your levels and then come back  down can actually facilitate more weight  loss as well and so I found that really  helpful but I kept to my fashion until  noon and running 30 minutes a day guys  when you persevere and it's hard and you  make it through and you win the victory  is just so much sweeter we number five  was no packaged foods and so I made a  decision apart from the coffee that  would have in the morning I wouldn't eat  anything from a package so nothing with  a wrapper nothing store-bought that was  not just processed but even healthy  stuff I wouldn't eat from a wrapper so  we need protein bars before and just  other things from packaged and decided  nope not gonna do it anymore  and most of my diet consists of fish we  don't really eat a lot of meat except on  Saturdays just fish and vegetables fish  vegetables nuts  mostly assortment of whitefish Cod  different filets haddock walleye bunch  of stuff Nina's been fantastic in  helping kind of  caryl the foods and it's great having a  partner on this journey so she's eaten  basically the same stuff I am  and then broccoli and cabbage and green  beans and sugar snap peas and it's  basically pretty easy to get filled up  because you're only really even two big  meals a day I would start usually at  noon eating a banana  - bananas probably two bananas sometimes  three bananas in the day and then into  my lunch and then into my dinner and  that would be it  I would snack on nuts and everything  basically not from a package trying to  trying to say healthy stratus a clean  and it's really helped with the weight  loss way number six is used My Fitness  Pal My Fitness Pal is an app that allows  you to track your calories and I'll load  it up here to show you guys so what you  can do is put in the foods can you see  can you see can you see anyway what you  can do is you they have goals this is a  free app that's put up by Under Armor I  think it's under armour you can put in  your goals of how high you are how like  how how high you are you pick how tall  you are what your goal is for weight and  how quickly you want to achieve it and  it'll give you a calorie target and then  you can enter in your food and it gives  you a sense of what every single meal  looks like and so if you're eating an  avocado you might think that's really  healthy but has a lot of calories and so  just being able to balance it out if you  are educated to know what is in your  food there are days that I will go to I  will go to Tim Hortons and get a crispy  chicken sandwich which is fried chicken  and bread and you know fairly high  calories like 540 calories something  like that but it fits it fits within my  day and so just educating yourself on  how many calories are in each meal is  great it has a barcode scanners so if  you are eatin